WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:05.000 --> 00:00:09.340
Republicans and Democrats differ significantly about the causes of climate change,

00:00:09.340 --> 00:00:12.599
its seriousness, and what ought to be done about it.

00:00:12.599 --> 00:00:18.180
85% of Democrats compared to 34% of
Republicans in an October CBS News poll

00:00:18.180 --> 00:00:22.890
say global warming is caused mostly by
human activity. In an NBC News/Wall

00:00:22.890 --> 00:00:27.900
Street Journal question from December,
71% of Democrats, but only 15% of

00:00:27.900 --> 00:00:31.679
Republicans said climate change has been
established ad serious and immediate

00:00:31.679 --> 00:00:35.880
action is necessary on it. In the Pew
Research Center's survey on political

00:00:35.880 --> 00:00:40.440
priorities that inquired about 18
possible priorities for President Trump

00:00:40.440 --> 00:00:44.820
and Congress, partisans differed more
about climate change that any other

00:00:44.820 --> 00:00:49.739
issue. 67 percent of Democrats but only
21 percent of Republicans said it should

00:00:49.739 --> 00:00:53.430
be a top priority this year. Although
differences are deep, there is some

00:00:53.430 --> 00:00:57.350
agreement among partisans on producing
domestic energy from different sources.

00:00:57.350 --> 00:01:01.410
Majorities in both parties agree that
more emphasis should be put on solar and

00:01:01.410 --> 00:01:05.400
wind. A plurality of Democrats and a
majority of Republicans wanted to put

00:01:05.400 --> 00:01:09.720
more emphasis on natural. Gas can
Republicans and Democrats come together

00:01:09.720 --> 00:01:14.430
on climate change? Let us know in our
poll. Also let us know what other topics

00:01:14.430 --> 00:01:18.540
you'd like our scholars to cover in 60
seconds and be sure to LIKE and

00:01:18.540 --> 00:01:23.119
subscribe for more research and videos
from AEI.

